// Canonical product catalogue (shared by listing + detail pages)
export const allProducts = [
  { slug: 'drywall-screws', image: '/images/products/drywall-screws-1.webp', pricePerPiece: 0.02, nameKey: 'drywall', specs: { size: '3.5-4.8mm × 25-100mm', standard: 'DIN 7505 / GB/T 15856', material: 'C1022 Carbon Steel', finish: 'Phosphate, Black Oxide' }, features: ['Sharp point', 'Bugle head', 'Fine thread', 'Wholesale supplier', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Construction', 'Interior decoration', 'Wood frame', 'Gypsum board', 'Wholesale bulk orders'], faq: ['What size drywall screw should I use? For 1/2-inch drywall on wood studs, use 1-5/8 inch screws. For 5/8-inch drywall, use 2-inch screws. For metal studs, use fine-thread drywall screws.', 'What is the difference between fine thread and coarse thread drywall screws? Fine thread screws are for metal studs (they grip metal better). Coarse thread screws are for wood studs (they bite into wood faster and hold better).', 'How many drywall screws do I need per sheet? Space screws every 12 inches on ceilings and every 16 inches on walls. A 4x8 sheet needs about 32-40 screws.', 'What is the bugle head on drywall screws? The bugle head has a concave shape that sits flush with the drywall paper without tearing it. Never use flat head screws on drywall.', 'Can drywall screws be used for outdoor projects? No, standard drywall screws (phosphate coated) are for indoor use only. For outdoor or wet areas, use stainless steel screws or exterior-rated fasteners.'] },
  { slug: 'self-drilling-screws', image: '/images/products/self-drilling-screws-1.webp', pricePerPiece: 0.03, nameKey: 'selfdrilling', specs: { size: '4.2-6.3mm × 19-150mm', standard: 'DIN 7504 / ANSI', material: 'C1022 Carbon Steel', finish: 'Zinc Plated, Ruspert' }, features: ['DR point', 'Hex/Phillips drive', 'Self-tapping', 'Metal-to-metal', 'Wholesale Tek screws', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Metal roofing', 'Steel structures', 'HVAC', 'Steel frame', 'Solar panel mounting', 'African construction', 'Wholesale bulk orders'], faq: ['What is a self-drilling screw? A self-drilling screw (tek screw) has a drill bit tip that drills its own hole and taps threads, eliminating the need for pre-drilling. Available in types 1-5, with type 3 being most common for metal roofing.', 'What is the difference between self-drilling and self-tapping screws? Self-drilling screws have a drill point that drills the hole; self-tapping screws require a pre-drilled hole. Self-drilling screws are faster for metal applications.', 'What size self-drilling screw for metal roofing? For metal roofing on steel purlins, typically use #10-16 or #12-14 self-drilling screws. Match screw length to combined thickness of roof sheet and purlin.', 'Can self-drilling screws be used for wood? Self-drilling screws are designed for metal-to-metal. For wood-to-metal, use self-tapping screws or wood screws. Self-drilling into wood may split the material.', 'What coatings are available for self-drilling screws in Africa? Common coatings: Zinc Plated (indoor/dry), Ruspert (alkaline resistant, outdoor), HDG Hot-Dip Galvanized (coastal/marine). For African coastal projects, use Ruspert or HDG coatings.', 'Do you supply self-drilling screws to African countries? Yes, we supply self-drilling screws to Zimbabwe, Zambia, South Africa, Mozambique via Durban and Beira ports. MOQ 100kg, lead time 15-25 days sea freight.'] },
  { slug: 'bolts-nuts', image: '/images/products/bolts-nuts-2.webp', pricePerPiece: 0.05, nameKey: 'bolts', specs: { size: 'M5-M30 × 20-300mm', standard: 'DIN 933/934 / ISO 4014', material: 'Q235/Q345 Steel', finish: 'Zinc, HDG, Black, YZP' }, features: ['Grade 4.8/8.8/10.9', 'Full/Partial thread', 'Various coatings', 'Hex bolts', 'Wholesale supplier'], applications: ['Construction', 'Machinery', 'Automotive', 'Industrial', 'Wholesale bulk orders'], faq: ['What is the difference between Grade 8.8 and Grade 10.9 bolts? Grade 8.8 bolts have minimum tensile strength of 800 MPa and are suitable for most construction applications. Grade 10.9 bolts have 1000 MPa tensile strength for high-stress structural applications. Grade 12.9 bolts (1200 MPa) are for specialized heavy-duty uses.', 'What is the difference between full thread and partial thread bolts? Full thread bolts have thread along the entire shaft, providing better tension and pull-out resistance. Partial thread bolts have an unthreaded shank portion that provides higher shear strength in the shank area. Choose full thread for tension loads, partial thread for shear-loaded connections.', 'What coating should I use for outdoor or coastal applications? For inland outdoor use, zinc-plated bolts provide adequate corrosion resistance. For coastal or marine environments (within 10km of saltwater), use hot-dip galvanized (HDG) or stainless steel 304/316 bolts. HDG provides cathodic protection and self-healing if damaged.', 'What is the minimum order quantity for bulk bolt orders? MOQ is typically 100-200 pieces per size for standard hex bolts. For mixed sizes or grades, MOQ may be 500-1000 pieces total. We welcome small orders for initial samples before larger bulk orders.', 'Do you supply metric bolts to African countries? Yes, we supply metric hex bolts M5-M36 to Zimbabwe, Zambia, South Africa, Mozambique, Kenya, and Nigeria via Durban, Beira, and Mombasa ports. Lead time 15-25 days sea freight. Grade 8.8 and 10.9 available with HDG or zinc finish.'] },
  { slug: 'ibr-nails', image: '/images/products/ibr-nails-1.webp', pricePerPiece: 0.01, nameKey: 'ibr', specs: { size: '2.5-4.0mm × 30-100mm', standard: 'SABS 1195', material: 'Q195/Q235 Wire', finish: 'Electro Galvanized' }, features: ['Umbrella head', 'Smooth/Ring shank', 'Roofing application', 'SABS certified', 'Wholesale supplier'], applications: ['Roofing', 'Cladding', 'Construction', 'IBR roof sheeting', 'Wholesale bulk orders'], faq: ['What are IBR nails used for? IBR nails (umbrella head nails) are specialized roofing nails with a large flat head designed for IBR (Inverted Box Rib) roof sheeting. The umbrella head provides excellent holding power and prevents water penetration through the roof sheet.', 'What is IBR nail size for roof installation? Standard IBR nail size is 3.45mm × 75mm or 3.75mm × 90mm. The nail should penetrate at least 25mm into the roof purlin or timber. Always check local building codes for specific requirements.', 'What is the difference between smooth shank and ring shank IBR nails? Ring shank IBR nails have rings on the shaft that provide superior withdrawal resistance, ideal for coastal areas or high-wind zones. Smooth shank nails are easier to drive but have lower pull-out resistance.', 'Are IBR nails SABS certified? Yes, our IBR nails are SABS 1195 certified, meeting South African Bureau of Standards requirements for roofing fasteners in Southern African development community (SADC) countries.', 'Do you supply IBR nails to African countries? Yes, we supply SABS-certified IBR nails to Zimbabwe, Zambia, South Africa, Mozambique, Namibia, and Botswana via Durban and Beira ports. MOQ 100kg, lead time 15-25 days sea freight.'] },
  { slug: 'anchor-bolts', image: '/images/products/anchor-bolts.webp', pricePerPiece: 0.12, nameKey: 'anchor', specs: { size: 'M10-M30 × 75-600mm', standard: 'DIN 529 / ASTM F1554 / SABS 153', material: 'Q235/Q345 Steel', finish: 'Hot-Dip Galvanized (HDG)', minOrder: '100 pcs' }, features: ['Heavy-duty', 'Foundation bolts', 'Structural connection', 'ASTM F1554 certified', 'HDG corrosion resistance', 'Wholesale supplier', 'ISO 9001 factory'], applications: ['Construction foundation', 'Steel structures', 'Solar panel mounting', 'Mining equipment', 'Bridge construction', 'Zimbabwe building projects'], faq: ['What is the lead time for anchor bolts to Zimbabwe? Lead time is 15-25 days by sea freight to Durban or Beira port.', 'What grades are available? Grade 4.6, 8.8, and 10.9 anchor bolts available with HDG finish.', 'Can you supply SABS certified anchor bolts? Yes, SABS 153 certified anchor bolts available for South Africa and Zimbabwe markets.', 'What is the minimum order quantity? MOQ is 100 pieces per size, mixed sizes welcome.', 'Do you provide custom lengths? Yes, custom lengths from 75mm to 600mm available with 7-day production time.'] },
  { slug: 'washers', image: '/images/products/washers.webp', pricePerPiece: 0.008, nameKey: 'washers', specs: { size: 'M6-M36', standard: 'DIN 125 / ISO 7089', material: 'Carbon Steel, Stainless Steel (304/316)', finish: 'Zinc Plated, HDG, Stainless Steel' }, features: ['Flat washers', 'Spring washers', 'Lock washers', 'Load distribution', 'Vibration resistance', 'Wholesale supplier', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Machinery', 'Automotive', 'Construction', 'Industrial assembly', 'Structural connections', 'Mining equipment', 'Wholesale bulk orders'], faq: ['What sizes of washers do you supply? We supply washers from M6 to M36, suitable for most construction and industrial applications. Flat washers (DIN 125/ISO 7089), spring washers (DIN 127), and lock washers (DIN 127B) available.', 'What materials are available for washers? Carbon steel with zinc plating or hot-dip galvanizing, and stainless steel 304/316 for corrosive environments. HDG washers recommended for African outdoor construction.', 'What is the difference between zinc-plated and hot-dip galvanized washers? Zinc-plated washers offer 5-8μm coating for indoor/dry environments. HDG washers have 45-85μm zinc coating for outdoor, coastal, and high-humidity African environments. Choose HDG for Zimbabwe and coastal applications.', 'Can washers be supplied with bolts and nuts? Yes, we offer bolt-washer-nut combo packages for construction and structural applications. Each combo is matched by size and grade for optimal performance. Combo pricing available for bulk orders.', 'What is the minimum order quantity for washers? MOQ is 500 pieces per size for standard washers. Mixed sizes welcome. For project orders over 10,000 pieces, contact us for volume pricing and dedicated production runs.', 'Do you supply spring washers (split lock washers)? Yes, spring washers available in both carbon steel (zinc plated) and stainless steel. Spring washers provide vibration resistance for dynamic load connections in machinery and structural applications.', 'What washer types are recommended for structural steel connections? For structural connections, use flat washers under both bolt head and nut to distribute load. Hardened washers (DIN 434/ISO 7413) are recommended for high-strength Grade 8.8 and 10.9 structural bolted connections.', 'Do you supply washers to African countries? Yes, we supply washers M6-M36 to Zimbabwe, Zambia, South Africa, Mozambique, Kenya, and Nigeria via Durban, Beira, and Mombasa ports. Lead time 15-25 days sea freight. HDG and stainless steel options for coastal regions.'] },
  { slug: 'coach-screws', image: '/images/products/coach-screws.webp', pricePerPiece: 0.025, nameKey: 'coach', specs: { size: 'M6-M12 × 30-200mm', standard: 'DIN 571 / LS 1993', material: 'Carbon Steel', finish: 'Hot-Dip Galvanized (HDG)' }, features: ['Hex head', 'Wood-to-wood', 'Deck screws', 'Heavy-duty', 'Outdoor use', 'HDG corrosion resistance', 'Wholesale supplier', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Decking', 'Fencing', 'Landscaping', 'Wood construction', 'Timber frame', 'Outdoor structures', 'Zimbabwe construction', 'Wholesale bulk orders'], faq: ['What is a coach screw used for? Coach screws (lag screws) are heavy-duty wood screws used for strong wood-to-wood connections in decking, fencing, and timber frame construction.', 'Are coach screws suitable for outdoor use? Yes, our coach screws are hot-dip galvanized (HDG) making them ideal for outdoor and corrosive environments.', 'What size coach screws do I need for decking? For deck joists, typically M8 × 80mm or M10 × 100mm coach screws are used. Check your local building codes for requirements.', 'Can coach screws be used with metal? Coach screws are primarily designed for wood-to-wood applications. For metal-to-wood, consider lag bolts or structural screws.', 'Do you supply coach screws to Zimbabwe? Yes, we supply HDG coach screws to Zimbabwe via Durban and Beira ports. Lead time 15-25 days by sea freight.', 'What is the difference between coach screws and wood screws? Coach screws (lag screws) have a hex head and require pre-drilling with a pilot hole. They provide much higher withdrawal resistance than standard wood screws, making them suitable for structural connections. Standard wood screws have a countersunk head and can self-tap.', 'What pilot hole size is needed for coach screws? For hardwoods, pre-drill 0.5mm smaller than the screw core diameter. For softwoods, pre-drill to the core diameter. The hex head sits flush when fully driven. Always check local building codes for specific requirements in your region.', 'Are coach screws suitable for Zimbabwe and Southern African construction? Yes, HDG coach screws are ideal for Southern African outdoor construction. They withstand high humidity and are SABS-compliant for structural timber connections in Zimbabwe, South Africa, Botswana, and Mozambique building projects.'] },
  { slug: 'threaded-rods', image: '/images/products/threaded-rods.webp', pricePerPiece: 0.08, nameKey: 'threaded', specs: { size: 'M6-M24 × 1m-3m', standard: 'DIN 975 / ISO 898', material: 'Carbon Steel / Stainless Steel 304/316', finish: 'Zinc Plated / HDG / Passivated', grade: 'Grade 4.8 / 8.8 / 10.9' }, features: ['Fully threaded', 'Custom lengths', 'Grade 8.8 / 10.9 available', 'Structural anchoring', 'Cut to size', 'HDG for outdoor use', 'Wholesale supplier', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Structural', 'Machinery', 'Assembly', 'Hanging systems', 'Solar panel mounting', 'Mining equipment', 'Water pipeline', 'Wholesale bulk orders'], faq: ['What is a threaded rod used for? Threaded rods (all-thread) are fully threaded bars used for structural anchoring, through-bolting, hanging systems, and tension rod applications in construction and machinery.', 'What sizes of threaded rods do you supply? We supply threaded rods from M6 to M24 diameter, in standard lengths of 1m, 2m, and 3m. Custom lengths from 500mm to 3m available on request.', 'Can threaded rods be cut to custom lengths? Yes, threaded rods can be easily cut to any custom length using a hacksaw or angle grinder. We also offer cut-to-size service for bulk orders.', 'What materials and grades are available? Standard material is carbon steel Grade 4.8 with zinc plating. High-strength Grade 8.8 and 10.9 available for structural applications. Stainless steel 304/316 for marine and corrosive environments.', 'What coating is recommended for outdoor African use? For outdoor African construction, specify hot-dip galvanized (HDG) threaded rods — the 45-85μm zinc coating provides cathodic protection ideal for high-humidity and coastal environments in Zimbabwe and coastal regions of Africa.', 'Do you supply threaded rods to African countries? Yes, we supply threaded rods to Zimbabwe, Zambia, South Africa, Mozambique via Durban and Beira ports. MOQ 50 pieces per size, lead time 15-25 days sea freight. Stainless steel and HDG options available for coastal projects.'] },
  { slug: 'chipboard-screws', image: '/images/products/timber-screws.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0.018, nameKey: 'chipboard', specs: { size: '3.5-5.0mm × 16-120mm', standard: 'DIN 7505 / EN 14566', material: 'C1022 Carbon Steel', finish: 'Yellow Zinc, White Zinc, Black Phosphate' }, features: ['Countersunk head', 'Pozi / Phillips drive', 'Coarse and fine thread', 'Ribbed under-head', 'Saw-thread option', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Particle board', 'Furniture assembly', 'Kitchen cabinets', 'Wooden pallets', 'Interior fit-out', 'Wholesale bulk orders'], faq: ['What is a chipboard screw used for? Chipboard screws (particle board screws) are countersunk wood screws with a coarse thread and a sharp point, designed to join particle board, MDF and softwood without splitting the board. They are the standard fastener for furniture, cabinets and shop fitting.', 'What size chipboard screw do I need for 18mm board? For joining 18mm particle board, use 4.0 × 50mm. As a rule the screw should reach about two-thirds into the second board — 3.5 × 40mm for 15mm board, 4.0 × 50mm for 18mm, 4.5 × 60mm for 25mm.', 'Do chipboard screws need pre-drilling? No, the sharp point and coarse thread let them self-tap into softwood and particle board. Near the edge of the board, or in hardwood, pre-drill a pilot hole to avoid splitting — roughly the core diameter of the screw.', 'What is the difference between coarse and fine thread chipboard screws? Coarse thread (single start) is for particle board, MDF and softwood, giving fast drive and high pull-out. Fine thread with a double start is for hardwood and for screwing close to edges, where it cuts cleaner and resists splitting.', 'Do you supply chipboard screws to African countries? Yes — we ship to Zimbabwe, Zambia, South Africa, Mozambique, Tanzania and Kenya via Durban, Beira and Mombasa. Standard packing is 1,000-5,000 pcs per carton, and mixed sizes can be loaded in one container.'] },
  { slug: 'concrete-screws', image: '/images/products/concrete-screws.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0.045, nameKey: 'concrete', specs: { size: '6.0-7.5mm × 40-200mm', standard: 'DIN 7504-K head / ETA assessment on request', material: 'Case-hardened carbon steel', finish: 'Yellow Zinc, White Zinc Galvanized' }, features: ['Self-cutting thread', 'No pre-drilling', 'Hex or Torx head', 'Removable anchor', 'High pull-out load', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Concrete fixing', 'Facade and cladding', 'Railings and handrails', 'Solar mounting', 'MEP supports', 'Wholesale bulk orders'], faq: ['What is a concrete screw? A concrete screw (concrete anchor screw) cuts its own thread into concrete as it is driven, so there is no drilling, no dust and no resin capsule. It holds by mechanical interlock and can be removed and reused in the same hole.', 'Which drill bit size do I need? The hole must match the screw: 6.0mm screw into a 6.0mm hole with a 6mm bit, 7.5mm screw into a 7.5mm hole. Too large a hole loses holding capacity, too small and the screw will not drive.', 'How deep should the screw go into concrete? The threaded portion must sit fully in the base material — for a 100mm screw that means roughly 50mm of thread in concrete. Minimum edge distance is about 1.5 times the anchor depth.', 'Can concrete screws be used in cracked concrete? Standard concrete screws are for uncracked concrete (typically C20/25 and above). For cracked concrete, specify anchors with an ETA assessment for cracked concrete — we can quote those on request.', 'Do you supply concrete screws to Zimbabwe and South Africa? Yes — 6.0mm and 7.5mm concrete screws ship regularly to Harare, Bulawayo, Lusaka and Johannesburg. MOQ 500 pcs per size, lead time 15-25 days by sea to Beira or Durban.'] },
  { slug: 'self-tapping-screws', image: '/images/products/self-tapping-screws.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0.015, nameKey: 'selftapping', specs: { size: '3.5-6.5mm × 9.5-200mm', standard: 'DIN 7985 / DIN 7504', material: 'C1022 / 1018 Carbon Steel', finish: 'Zinc Plated, Black Oxide, Ruspert' }, features: ['Pan / wafer / countersunk / oval heads', 'Cross, Pozi or Torx drive', 'Sharp point for sheet metal and wood', 'Washer-head option', 'Colour-matched heads on request', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Sheet metal assembly', 'Electrical enclosures', 'HVAC ducting', 'Appliance assembly', 'General workshop use', 'Wholesale bulk orders'], faq: ['What is the difference between self-tapping and self-drilling screws? Self-tapping screws need a pre-drilled hole and cut their own thread into it. Self-drilling (TEK) screws carry a drill point and do both in one pass. For thin sheet metal and plastics, self-tapping is usually cheaper and sufficient.', 'Which head type should I specify? Pan head for general assembly, wafer head for a low profile over thin sheet, countersunk for flush finish, oval head for a decorative finish. Washer heads spread load on soft or thin material.', 'What thread pitch do I need for sheet metal? Fine pitch (more threads per inch) for thin sheet, coarse pitch for thicker material and plastics. Tell us the sheet thickness and we will match the pitch.', 'Are these screws available in stainless steel? Yes — A2 (304) and A4 (316) stainless versions are available for coastal and food-grade applications, at higher cost than zinc-plated steel.', 'Do you supply self-tapping screws to African countries? Yes — to Zimbabwe, Zambia, South Africa, Mozambique and Kenya. Bulk cartons of 1,000-5,000 pcs, mixed sizes per container, 15-25 days sea freight.'] },
  { slug: 'blind-rivets', image: '/images/products/rivets.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0.012, nameKey: 'rivets', specs: { size: '3.2 / 4.0 / 4.8 / 6.4mm diameter', standard: 'DIN 7337', material: 'Aluminium 5052, Steel, Stainless 304', finish: 'Mill, Painted, Zinc Plated' }, features: ['Large flange option', 'Countersunk head', 'Structural multi-grip rivets', 'One-side fastening', 'Colour-painted heads', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Roof sheeting', 'Gutters and flashings', 'Truck and trailer bodies', 'Signage', 'Appliances', 'Wholesale bulk orders'], faq: ['How does a blind rivet work? The rivet is placed in a drilled hole and a riveting tool pulls the mandrel through, expanding the rivet body on the far side. It fastens from one side only — ideal where you cannot reach behind the panel.', 'Which rivet size for a given hole? Match the rivet diameter to the hole: 3.2mm rivet = 3.2mm hole, 4.8mm rivet = 4.8mm hole. The rivet length must cover the combined thickness of both sheets plus a little for expansion.', 'What is the difference between aluminium and steel rivets? Aluminium is light and easy to set, used for roofing, gutters and light sheet. Steel and stainless carry much higher shear strength for structural and load-bearing joints, and stainless resists corrosion at the coast.', 'What are structural (multi-grip) rivets? Structural rivets lock mechanically and stay load-bearing even if the mandrel is lost — they are specified where vibration or safety matters, such as truck bodies and structural steel sheet.', 'Do you supply blind rivets to African countries? Yes — Zimbabwe, Zambia, South Africa, Mozambique, Tanzania and Kenya. Standard box 1,000 pcs, mixed sizes per carton, 15-25 days by sea.'] },
  { slug: 'coil-nails', image: '/images/products/coil-nails.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0.008, nameKey: 'coilnails', specs: { size: '2.5-3.3mm × 50-90mm', standard: 'EN 10230-1', material: 'Q195 / Q235 Wire', finish: 'Bright, Electro Galvanized, HDG' }, features: ['15° / 21° / 28° collation', 'Smooth or ring shank', 'Paper or plastic collation', 'Framing nailer compatible', 'Bulk coil packing', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Timber framing', 'Pallets and crates', 'Fencing', 'Batten installation', 'Truss assembly', 'Wholesale bulk orders'], faq: ['What are coil nails? Coil nails (collated framing nails) are strip-glued at a fixed angle so they feed from a coil into a pneumatic framing nailer. They let one operator drive hundreds of nails an hour without hand feeding.', 'What collation angle do I need? Collation angle must match your nailer: 15° for most stick/coil framing nailers, 21° and 28° for other brands. Tell us the tool model and we will match the angle and strip.', 'What is the difference between smooth and ring shank coil nails? Ring shank nails have annular rings that raise withdrawal resistance — preferred for pallets, crates and anything that vibrates. Smooth shank drives faster and is cheaper for static framing.', 'Which nails for pallet production? Typically 2.5-2.8mm × 63-75mm ring shank, or 3.1mm × 80-90mm for heavier pallets. Galvanized finish is preferred where pallets are stored outdoors.', 'Do you supply coil nails to African countries? Yes — Zimbabwe, Zambia, South Africa and Mozambique. Coils are packed in cartons of 1,000-4,000 pcs depending on size, 15-25 days by sea.'] },
  { slug: 'common-nails', image: '/images/products/common-nails.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0.006, nameKey: 'commonnails', specs: { size: '2.0-6.0mm × 25-200mm (1″-8″)', standard: 'EN 10230-1', material: 'Q195 / Q235 Wire', finish: 'Bright, Electro Galvanized, HDG' }, features: ['Flat round head', 'Smooth or ring shank', 'Diamond point', 'Clout and duplex versions', '25kg carton packing', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Timber construction', 'Packaging and crates', 'Fencing', 'Roofing battens', 'General site work', 'Wholesale bulk orders'], faq: ['What are common nails used for? Common nails (flat-head wire nails) are the general-purpose construction nail — timber framing, packaging, crates, fencing and general site work. They are driven with a hammer and hold by friction and shank deformation.', 'Which nail size for which job? 2″-3″ (50-75mm) for light boxing and packaging, 3″-4″ (75-100mm) for battens and fencing, 4″-6″ (100-150mm) for structural timber. A nail should be about three times the thickness of the piece it passes through.', 'What is the difference between bright and galvanized nails? Bright (uncoated) nails are cheapest and fine indoors or where they will be painted over. Electro-galvanized gives light protection outdoors; hot-dip galvanized is for fencing, coastal work and anywhere the nail stays exposed to weather.', 'Can you supply clout and duplex nails? Yes — clout nails (large flat head for roofing felt and sheeting) and duplex nails (double head, easy to pull out of temporary formwork) are both available in the same cartons.', 'Do you supply common nails to African countries? Yes — 25kg cartons to Zimbabwe, Zambia, South Africa and Mozambique, mixed sizes per pallet, 15-25 days by sea to Beira or Durban.'] },
  { slug: 'sleeve-anchors', image: '/images/products/sleeve-anchors.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0.15, nameKey: 'sleeveanchor', specs: { size: 'M6-M20 × 40-200mm', standard: 'ETA / ETAG 001 assessment on request', material: 'Stainless 304 / 316, Zinc-plated carbon steel', finish: 'Mill (stainless), Zinc Plated' }, features: ['Hex nut and washer included', 'Expansion sleeve', 'Stainless for coastal work', 'Through-fastening option', 'Drop-in and wedge versions', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Concrete and brick fixing', 'Balustrades and railings', 'Canopies and carports', 'Solar mounting', 'Coastal and marine sites', 'Wholesale bulk orders'], faq: ['What is a sleeve anchor? A sleeve anchor has a tapered mandrel inside an expanding sleeve. Tightening the nut pulls the mandrel up and expands the sleeve against the hole wall, locking into concrete, brick or block.', 'When should I specify stainless instead of zinc-plated? Anywhere the anchor stays exposed outdoors, and always within about 10km of the coast or in chemical plants. A4 (316) stainless is the safe choice for Zimbabwe mining sites, Mozambican ports and coastal Kenya.', 'What hole size do I drill? Drill the nominal anchor diameter: M8 anchor into an 8mm hole, M10 into 10mm. Hole depth should exceed the anchor’s embedded length by about 10mm so debris does not stop the anchor short.', 'What is the difference between sleeve, wedge and drop-in anchors? Sleeve expands along its length for general concrete and brick. Wedge anchors are for hard, uncracked concrete and heavy loads. Drop-in anchors sit flush in a pre-drilled hole for suspended services such as conduit and pipe hangers.', 'Do you supply sleeve anchors to African countries? Yes — M6 to M20, stainless and zinc-plated, to Zimbabwe, Zambia, South Africa, Mozambique and Kenya. MOQ 200 pcs per size, 15-25 days by sea.'] },
  { slug: 'expansion-bolts', image: '/images/products/expansion-bolts.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0.09, nameKey: 'expansion', specs: { size: 'M6-M24 × 50-300mm', standard: 'GB/T 22795 / ETA assessment on request', material: 'Carbon Steel, Stainless 304 / 316', finish: 'Yellow Zinc, HDG, Stainless' }, features: ['Wedge-type expansion', 'Hex head with washer', 'Flange nut option', 'Custom lengths', 'HDG for outdoor use', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Structural fixing', 'Steel column base plates', 'Pipe supports', 'Air-conditioning units', 'Fencing posts', 'Wholesale bulk orders'], faq: ['What is an expansion bolt? An expansion bolt (wedge anchor) has a wedge at the bottom that is pulled up as the nut is tightened, forcing the sleeve or wedge to grip the concrete. It is the standard heavy-duty fixing for structural and equipment anchoring.', 'Which size for a given load? M8-M10 for pipe supports and light equipment, M12-M16 for steel base plates and heavy units, M20-M24 for structural columns. Tell us the load and substrate and we will suggest the size.', 'How deep must the anchor be embedded? The threaded expansion section should sit fully in the concrete — typically 60-80mm for M10, 80-100mm for M16. Minimum edge distance is about 1.5 times the embedded depth.', 'What finish for outdoor sites in Zimbabwe? Hot-dip galvanized (HDG) for exposed outdoor anchoring, or stainless 304/316 near the coast and at mine sites where sulphates and humidity attack zinc coatings quickly.', 'Do you supply expansion bolts to African countries? Yes — M6 to M24, zinc-plated, HDG and stainless, to Zimbabwe, Zambia, South Africa and Mozambique. MOQ 200 pcs per size, 15-25 days by sea.'] },
  { slug: 'concrete-nails', image: '/images/products/concrete-nails.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0.007, nameKey: 'concretenails', specs: { size: '2.0-5.0mm x 25-125mm (1"-5")', standard: 'EN 10230-1 / GB/T 349', material: '60# / 70# high-carbon steel', finish: 'Blue-black (heat treated), Zinc Plated' }, features: ['Hardened high-carbon shank', 'Flat round head', 'Drives into concrete and masonry', 'No cartridge or tool needed', '25kg carton packing', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Concrete and masonry', 'Formwork and shuttering', 'Door and window frames', 'Site setting out', 'Wholesale bulk orders'], faq: ['What is a concrete nail? A concrete nail (masonry nail) is a hardened high-carbon steel nail with a flat round head, driven straight into concrete, mortar or brick without a plastic plug or powder cartridge.', 'What size concrete nail do I need? 1"-1.5" (25-40 mm) for fixing timber battens and trunking, 2"-3" (50-75 mm) for door frames and formwork, 4"-5" (100-125 mm) for heavy timber into blockwork. The nail should penetrate about twice the thickness of the part it fixes.', 'Do concrete nails need a pilot hole? In old, hard concrete a 2 mm pilot hole helps and stops the head mushrooming; in block and mortar the nail drives directly. Always wear eye protection, as concrete nails can chip the surface.', 'Why do concrete nails break? They are hardened, so they snap if bent sideways or driven into aggregate. Drive them straight; if a nail hits stone, withdraw it and move 20-30 mm along.', 'Do you supply concrete nails to Zimbabwe? Yes - 25 kg cartons, 1"-5", blue-black or zinc plated, to Zimbabwe, Zambia, South Africa and Mozambique, 15-25 days by sea.'] },

  { slug: 'shooting-nails', image: '/images/products/shooting-nails.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0.02, nameKey: 'shootingnails', specs: { size: '3.0-4.5mm x 19-72mm', standard: 'EN 10230-1 / GB/T 18981', material: 'High-carbon steel, hardened core', finish: 'Zinc Plated, red plastic collar' }, features: ['Red fluted collar', 'Hardened core pin', 'Fastens Q235 steel 0.8-1.2mm', 'No drilling, no dust', 'Boxed 1,000 pcs', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Steel plate fixing', 'Concrete fixing', 'Ceiling hangers', 'Duct and pipe supports', 'Formwork bracing'], faq: ['What is a shooting nail? A shooting nail is a powder-actuated fastener - a hardened pin with a plastic collar driven into concrete or steel by a cartridge tool, with no drilling and no dust.', 'What base materials can it fasten? Q235 steel plate 0.8-1.2 mm and concrete grade C20 and above. It will not hold in thin sheet, timber or hollow block.', 'Which collar colour for which job? The collar centres the pin and seals the hole - red for concrete, blue or black for steel in most systems. Match the collar to the tool and base material recommended by the tool maker.', 'Is a licence needed to use powder-actuated tools? Yes in most countries - operators must be trained and certified, and hearing and eye protection are mandatory. We supply the fasteners only, not the tools or cartridges.', 'Do you supply shooting nails to Africa? Yes - boxed 1,000 pcs, 3.0-4.5 mm x 19-72 mm, to Zimbabwe, Zambia and South Africa, 15-25 days by sea.'] },

  { slug: 'clout-nails', image: '/images/products/clout-nails.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0.006, nameKey: 'cloutnails', specs: { size: '2.0-3.5mm x 19-75mm', standard: 'EN 10230-1', material: 'Q195 / Q235 wire', finish: 'Electro Galvanized, HDG' }, features: ['Wide flat head', 'Short shank', 'Holds felt and membrane', 'Smooth or ring shank', '25kg carton packing', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Roofing felt', 'Waterproof membrane', 'Underlay and insulation board', 'Box and crate lining', 'Gutter and flashing'], faq: ['What is a clout nail? A clout nail has a wide flat head and short shank, made for fixing roofing felt, waterproof membrane, underlay and insulation board, where a large head must hold a soft sheet.', 'Which size for roofing felt? 19-25 mm for felt and membrane, 30-40 mm for insulation board and sheathing, 50-75 mm for battens. The head should overlap the sheet without tearing it.', 'Galvanized or bright? Electro-galvanized for general outdoor roofing, hot-dip galvanized for coastal and long-life roofs. Bright is for indoor lining and boxing only.', 'Smooth or ring shank? Ring shank clout nails hold far better in timber battens and are the safer choice for wind uplift; smooth shank drives faster and is cheaper for temporary work.', 'Do you supply clout nails to Zimbabwe? Yes - 25 kg cartons, 2.0-3.5 mm x 19-75 mm, galvanized, 15-25 days by sea to Beira or Durban.'] },

  { slug: 'duplex-nails', image: '/images/products/duplex-nails.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0.009, nameKey: 'duplexnails', specs: { size: '2.8-4.0mm x 50-100mm', standard: 'EN 10230-1', material: 'Q195 / Q235 wire', finish: 'Bright, Electro Galvanized' }, features: ['Double head design', 'Easy pull-out', 'Re-usable in formwork', 'Smooth shank', '25kg carton packing', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Scaffold boards', 'Formwork and shuttering', 'Temporary structures', 'Fencing panels', 'Site concreting'], faq: ['What is a duplex nail? A duplex nail has two heads - the lower head drives the timber, the upper head stays proud so the nail can be pulled out with a claw hammer without damaging the board.', 'Where are duplex nails used? Scaffold boards, formwork, temporary bracing, fencing panels and any assembly that has to be struck and re-used.', 'What size for scaffold boards? 3.0-3.5 mm x 65-75 mm is the common scaffold board size; 50 mm for lighter formwork, 90-100 mm for thick timber.', 'Are duplex nails reusable? Yes - that is the point. The double head lets them be withdrawn and driven again several times, though the shank eventually fatigues at the lower head.', 'Do you supply duplex nails to Zimbabwe? Yes - 25 kg cartons, bright or electro-galvanized, 15-25 days by sea.'] },

  { slug: 'wedge-anchors', image: '/images/products/wedge-anchors.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0.22, nameKey: 'wedgeanchor', specs: { size: 'M6-M20 x 40-160mm', standard: 'ETA / ETAG 001 assessment on request', material: 'SS304 / SS316, zinc-plated carbon steel', finish: 'Mill (stainless), Zinc Plated' }, features: ['Wedge expansion at base', 'Hex nut and washer included', 'High load in hard concrete', 'Stainless for coastal sites', 'Permanent fixing', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Structural base plates', 'Racking and shelving', 'Pipe and duct supports', 'Balustrades and handrails', 'Mine and coastal sites'], faq: ['What is a wedge anchor? A wedge anchor carries a tapered wedge at the bottom; tightening the nut pulls the wedge into the clip and expands it against the hole wall, giving a very high load in hard concrete.', 'Wedge, sleeve or drop-in - which one? Wedge for uncracked structural concrete and heavy loads; sleeve for general concrete and brick; drop-in for flush fixing of suspended services.', 'What embedment depth? Minimum 60-80 mm for M10, 80-100 mm for M16, and edge distance at least 1.5 times the embedment. Follow the anchor chart for the load required.', 'Can a wedge anchor be removed? Once set it is permanent - cut flush if it must go. If removal is likely, use a sleeve or bolt anchor instead.', 'Do you supply wedge anchors in stainless? Yes - SS304 and SS316, M6-M20, for coastal, mine and food-plant sites; zinc-plated carbon steel for inland dry use.'] },

  { slug: 'drop-in-anchors', image: '/images/products/drop-in-anchors.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0.06, nameKey: 'dropinanchor', specs: { size: 'M6-M20 x 25-50mm', standard: 'ETA / ETAG 001 assessment on request', material: 'Zinc-plated carbon steel, SS304 / SS316', finish: 'Zinc Plated, Stainless' }, features: ['Internal thread socket', 'Flush finish, no protrusion', 'Four expansion lips', 'Set with a hand tool', 'For suspended services', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Conduit and cable tray', 'Pipe hangers', 'Fire sprinkler supports', 'Duct suspension', 'Ceiling grids'], faq: ['What is a drop-in anchor? A drop-in anchor is a flush, internally threaded sleeve set into a drilled hole; a machine screw or threaded rod then fixes into it, leaving no protrusion.', 'How is it set? Drive it to depth with the setting tool so the punch expands the lips; the thread must stay clean and the hole must be blown free of dust before setting.', 'Where is it used? Suspended conduit, cable tray, pipe hangers, fire sprinkler and duct supports - anything where a flush threaded socket in a soffit is wanted.', 'What size for M8 rod? Use an M8 drop-in with an 8 mm screw; hole diameter 14 mm, minimum depth 40 mm. Match the anchor thread to the rod, not the hole.', 'Do you supply drop-in anchors to Zimbabwe? Yes - M6-M20, zinc-plated or stainless, boxed 100-200 pcs, 15-25 days by sea.'] },

  { slug: 'set-anchors', image: '/images/products/set-anchors.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0.05, nameKey: 'setanchor', specs: { size: 'M6-M16 x 25-65mm', standard: 'SS201 / SS304 series, ETA on request', material: 'Stainless 201 / 304, zinc-plated carbon steel', finish: 'Mill (stainless), Zinc Plated' }, features: ['Machine screw inside sleeve', 'Short embedment depth', 'Quick setting', 'Corrosion-resistant options', 'Screw supplied with anchor', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Light fixtures', 'Electrical boxes', 'Signage and brackets', 'Handrail base plates', 'Interior fit-out'], faq: ['What is a set anchor? A set anchor (machine screw anchor) is a short stainless or zinc-plated sleeve that expands as its inner screw is driven, giving a quick fixing into concrete or brick.', 'Set anchor or drop-in? The set anchor comes with its own screw and sets by driving it home; the drop-in is an empty threaded socket for a separate screw or rod. Choose by whether you want the screw supplied.', 'What sizes? M6-M16 x 25-65 mm covers most fixtures; SS201 for dry indoor work, SS304 or SS316 for wet and coastal sites.', 'Can it be used in brick? Yes in solid brick and block, but reduce the working load by about half compared with concrete. Not for hollow block or aerated block.', 'Do you supply set anchors to African countries? Yes - stainless SS201/304, boxed, 15-25 days by sea to Beira or Durban.'] },

  { slug: 'bolt-anchors', image: '/images/products/bolt-anchors.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0.14, nameKey: 'boltanchor', specs: { size: 'M6-M20 x 50-200mm', standard: 'ETA / ETAG 001 assessment on request', material: 'Zinc-plated carbon steel, SS304 / SS316', finish: 'Yellow Zinc, HDG, Stainless' }, features: ['Through-bolt fixing', 'Sleeve expansion', 'Nut and washer included', 'Clamps the fixture', 'Heavy-duty anchoring', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Steel column base plates', 'Racking and pallet racks', 'Pipe supports', 'Air-conditioning units', 'Fencing posts'], faq: ['What is a bolt anchor? A bolt anchor combines a hex bolt with an expanding sleeve; the bolt passes through the fixture, and tightening the nut expands the sleeve in the concrete.', 'Bolt anchor or expansion bolt? They are the same family - the bolt anchor is the through-fixing version supplied with nut and washer, used where the fixture is clamped between the head and the concrete.', 'What size for a base plate? M10-M12 for light racking and pipe supports, M16-M20 for steel columns and heavy equipment. Check the anchor chart for tension and shear load.', 'What finish for outdoor use in Africa? Yellow zinc for sheltered inland sites, hot-dip galvanized or stainless 304/316 for exposed, coastal and mine sites.', 'Do you supply bolt anchors to Zimbabwe? Yes - M6-M20 x 50-200 mm, zinc-plated or stainless, MOQ 200 pcs per size, 15-25 days by sea.'] },

  { slug: 'butyl-tape', image: '/images/products/butyl-tape.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0.5, nameKey: 'butyltape', minOrder: '500 kg', leadTime: '20-25 days', specs: { size: '50-300mm wide x 5-20m roll', standard: 'GB/T 23457 / ASTM D1970', material: 'Butyl rubber with aluminium foil facing', finish: 'Black compound, aluminium face' }, features: ['Permanently flexible', 'Aluminium foil facing', 'Pressure-bond, no torch', 'Seals laps and upstands', 'Rolls 5-20 m', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Roof laps and flashings', 'Gutter and upstand junctions', 'Window and wall sealing', 'Vapour barrier joints', 'Metal sheet laps'], faq: ['What is butyl tape used for? Butyl tape is a permanently flexible sealing strip for joints in roofing, gutters, flashings, window and wall junctions, and for sealing under metal sheets and vapour barriers.', 'How is it applied? Clean and dry the surface, peel the release paper, press the tape into the joint and roll it down hard. It bonds by pressure and stays flexible, so it follows thermal movement.', 'What width do I need? 50 mm for laps and small joints, 100-150 mm for gutter and upstand junctions, 200-300 mm for wide flashings and parapets.', 'Will it work in hot African climates? Yes - butyl rubber keeps its flexibility at high temperature, and the aluminium foil facing reflects sun and protects the compound. Avoid applying to wet or dusty surfaces.', 'Do you supply butyl tape to Zimbabwe? Yes - rolls of 5-20 m in 50-300 mm widths, MOQ 500 kg, 20-25 days by sea.'] },

  { slug: 'asphalt-flash-band', image: '/images/products/asphalt-flash-band.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0.4, nameKey: 'flashband', minOrder: '500 kg', leadTime: '20-25 days', specs: { size: '50-500mm wide x 5-15m roll', standard: 'GB/T 23457', material: 'SBS asphalt with aluminium foil facing', finish: 'Silver aluminium face, bitumen backing' }, features: ['Self-adhesive, peel and stick', 'Aluminium-faced', 'For repair and patching', 'Cuts with a knife', 'Rolls 5-15 m', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Roof repairs and laps', 'Gutter and valley sealing', 'Pipe penetrations', 'Cracked felt patching', 'Parapet flashings'], faq: ['What is flash band? Flash band is an aluminium-faced, bitumen-backed self-adhesive strip for patching and sealing flashings, gutters, roof laps, pipe penetrations and cracked felt.', 'Flash band or butyl tape? Flash band is the cheaper, stiffer repair tape for roofs and gutters; butyl tape is softer and stays flexible longer, better for movement joints and long-term sealing.', 'How do I apply it? Wire-brush and dry the surface, cut the strip, peel the backing and press it down, then dress the edges with a roller. Overlap ends by at least 50 mm.', 'Is it UV stable? The aluminium facing reflects most UV; on long exposed runs a coated or painted top coat extends life. It is not a substitute for a proper membrane on a new roof.', 'Do you supply flash band to Africa? Yes - 50-500 mm widths, 5-15 m rolls, MOQ 500 kg, 20-25 days by sea.'] },

  { slug: 'non-woven-fabric', image: '/images/products/non-woven-fabric.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0.3, nameKey: 'nonwoven', minOrder: '500 kg', leadTime: '20-25 days', specs: { size: '1.0-3.0m wide x 50-100m roll, 30-150 gsm', standard: 'GB/T 24218', material: 'Polypropylene (PP) spunbond', finish: 'White, black, colours on request' }, features: ['Spunbond PP', '30-150 gsm range', 'Reinforcement and separation', 'Roll widths to 3 m', 'UV grades on request', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Waterproofing carrier', 'Geotextile separation', 'Filtration layer', 'Covers and bags', 'Packaging'], faq: ['What is the non-woven fabric used for? PP spunbond non-woven is used as a carrier and reinforcement in waterproofing, as a separation and filtration layer, and for bags, covers and packaging.', 'What weight do I need? 30-60 gsm for packaging and covers, 80-120 gsm for waterproofing reinforcement and geotextile separation, 150 gsm and above for heavy-duty covers.', 'Is it UV stabilised? Standard white fabric is not; for outdoor covers specify UV-stabilised black or coloured grades, which we quote on request.', 'Can it be laminated or coated? Yes - the fabric can be supplied for bitumen or membrane lamination; tell us the process and we will match the weight and width.', 'Do you supply non-woven fabric to Africa? Yes - rolls 1.0-3.0 m wide x 50-100 m, MOQ 500 kg, 20-25 days by sea.'] },

  { slug: 'waterproof-coating', image: '/images/products/waterproof-coating.jpg', pricePerPiece: 2.5, nameKey: 'wproofcoating', minOrder: '500 kg', leadTime: '20-25 days', specs: { size: '5-20 kg pail', standard: 'JC/T 408 / GB/T 19250', material: 'Polyurethane / rubber asphalt / acrylic', finish: 'Grey, black or colour on request' }, features: ['Liquid-applied membrane', 'Seamless, no joints', 'One or two component', 'Brush, roller or spray', '5-20 kg pails', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Flat roofs', 'Basement and retaining walls', 'Wet rooms and shower areas', 'Balconies and podiums', 'Repair over old bitumen'], faq: ['What is waterproof coating? A liquid-applied membrane - polyurethane, rubber asphalt or acrylic - brushed or rolled on and cured to a seamless waterproof layer for roofs, basements and wet areas.', 'Which type for which job? Polyurethane for exposed roofs and heavy traffic, rubber asphalt for basements and repair work, acrylic for walls and light roofs. One-component for small jobs, two-component for demanding ones.', 'How many coats? Two coats at right angles, about 1.5 kg/m2 total, with the first coat dry before the second. Coverage figures vary by product and are stated on the pail.', 'Can it be applied over old bitumen? Yes after cleaning and priming, but loose or blistered material must be removed first. Do not apply over damp surfaces or standing water.', 'Do you supply waterproof coating to Zimbabwe? Yes - 5-20 kg pails, MOQ 500 kg, 20-25 days by sea.'] },

  { slug: 'waterproof-membrane', image: '/images/products/waterproof-membrane.jpg', pricePerPiece: 3.2, nameKey: 'wmembrane', minOrder: '500 kg', leadTime: '20-25 days', specs: { size: '1.0-2.0m x 10-20m roll, 3-4mm', standard: 'GB 18242 / GB 12952', material: 'SBS modified bitumen, PVC / TPO', finish: 'Sand surfaced, mineral or foil faced' }, features: ['Factory-controlled thickness', 'SBS torch-on or single-ply', 'Laps 100 mm', 'For roofs and basements', 'Rolls 10-20 m', 'ISO 9001 certified'], applications: ['Flat and podium roofs', 'Basement tanking', 'Ponds and reservoirs', 'Car park decks', 'Refurbishment over felt'], faq: ['What is a waterproof membrane? A factory-made sheet - SBS modified bitumen, PVC or TPO - laid over roofs and basements to form a continuous, thickness-controlled waterproof layer.', 'SBS or PVC/TPO? SBS torch-on is the workhorse for flat roofs and cheapest per m2; PVC and TPO are single-ply, weldable, and better for large roofs, ponds and exposed UV.', 'How is SBS membrane installed? Torch-applied over a primed substrate with laps of at least 100 mm. Check local fire rules - torch-on is restricted on some sites and cold adhesive can be used instead.', 'What thickness? 3 mm for refurbishment over existing felt, 4 mm for new flat roofs and podiums, 5 mm for heavy traffic and protected membrane roofs.', 'Do you supply waterproof membrane to Africa? Yes - 1.0-2.0 m x 10-20 m rolls, 3-4 mm, MOQ 500 kg, 20-25 days by sea.'] },



  { slug: 'u-bolts', image: '/images/products/u-bolts.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'ubolts', minOrder: '1 ton', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: 'M6-M30, thread length 30-150 mm', standard: 'DIN 3570 / GB/T 5976', material: 'Q235B, 35#, 45# carbon steel; SS304/316', finish: 'HDG, electro-galvanized, plain' }, features: ['Round, square and long-neck bends', 'Nuts and steel plate supplied as a set', 'HDG for outdoor and coastal sites', 'Bending radius matched to pipe OD', 'Made to drawing for non-standard sizes'], applications: ['Water and gas pipe clamping', 'Pole and mast fixing', 'Vehicle axle and leaf spring', 'Signage and guardrail brackets', 'Solar and antenna mounts'], faq: ['What is a U-bolt used for? It clamps a pipe, tube or pole against a flat support - the two legs pass through a plate or bracket and are tightened with nuts, so the load is carried by the bend, not the thread.', 'How do I size a U-bolt? Match the inner width to the outside diameter of the pipe, then choose thread length so that the nut and plate sit on the support. DIN 3570 lists inner width, bend radius and thread length for each size.', 'Which finish for outdoor sites? Hot-dip galvanizing to ISO 1461 for general outdoor use; SS304 for humid inland sites and SS316 where chlorides or coastal salt spray are present.'] },
  { slug: 'eye-bolts', image: '/images/products/eye-bolts.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'eyebolts', minOrder: '1 ton', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: 'M8-M24, thread 20-60 mm', standard: 'DIN 580 / DIN 581', material: 'C15E forged carbon steel; SS304/316', finish: 'HDG, electro-galvanized, self-colour' }, features: ['Forged eye, not cast', 'Proof-load marked where required', 'Full thread to DIN 580', 'Swivel and metric-thread variants', 'Supplied with or without nut'], applications: ['Lifting and slinging', 'Rigging and hoisting gear', 'Tie-down points on trailers', 'Cable and rope anchoring', 'Workshop and warehouse fixtures'], faq: ['Are eye bolts rated for lifting? Only eye bolts supplied and marked as lifting equipment should be used overhead. General DIN 580 eye bolts are for guiding and tie-down unless a proof load and working load limit are stated.', 'DIN 580 or DIN 581? DIN 580 has the eye in line with the thread and is for straight pull; DIN 581 has a larger eye and is used with a swivel for angled loads.', 'Can they be used outdoors? Yes - specify HDG or stainless. Zinc-plated eye bolts lose coating quickly on coastal or humid sites.'] },
  { slug: 'foundation-bolts', image: '/images/products/foundation-bolts.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'foundationbolts', minOrder: '1 ton', leadTime: '20-25 days', specs: { size: 'M12-M36, length 300-1500 mm', standard: 'GB/T 799, project drawings', material: 'Q235B, 35#, grade 8.8', finish: 'Plain, HDG, zinc rich primer' }, features: ['Straight, L-bend and plate types', 'Cut to drawing length', 'Thread protected during shipping', 'Nuts and washers supplied loose', 'Batch traceability on request'], applications: ['Steel structure column bases', 'Warehouse and factory frames', 'Transmission towers', 'Equipment and machine bases', 'Precast panel connections'], faq: ['What is a foundation bolt? A bolt cast into concrete or grouted into a base that carries the column or machine load, usually with an L-bend or anchor plate so it cannot pull out.', 'How long should the embedment be? A common starting point is 20-25 times the bolt diameter for a straight shank in good concrete, longer for L-bends and short embedments; the structural engineer\'s drawing governs.', 'How are they protected in transit? Threads are greased and wrapped, and bundles are strapped by length so that site fixing matches the drawing.'] },
  { slug: 'carriage-bolts', image: '/images/products/carriage-bolts.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'carriagebolts', minOrder: '1 ton', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: 'M6-M20, 25-300 mm', standard: 'DIN 603 / ANSI B18.5', material: 'C1022, grade 4.8/8.8; SS304', finish: 'HDG, electro-galvanized, plain' }, features: ['Square neck locks into timber', 'Cup head leaves a smooth face', 'No head-side wrench needed', 'Full and part thread options', 'HDG for outdoor timber structures'], applications: ['Timber framing and decking', 'Fence and gate building', 'Playground and bench assembly', 'Trailer and truck bodies', 'Steel-to-timber connections'], faq: ['Why does a carriage bolt have a square neck? The square shoulder bites into the timber so the bolt cannot rotate when the nut is tightened from the other side, and the smooth dome head is left exposed.', 'Do I need a washer? Yes, a washer under the nut spreads the load and stops it sinking into softwood; for HDG work use HDG washers to avoid bimetallic corrosion.', 'Can carriage bolts be used in steel? They can, but the square neck must sit in a square hole; for plain steel plate a hex bolt is the normal choice.'] },
  { slug: 'allen-bolts', image: '/images/products/allen-bolts.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'allenbolts', minOrder: '1 ton', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: 'M6-M24, 20-200 mm', standard: 'DIN 912 / ISO 4762', material: 'SCM435 alloy steel; SS304/316', finish: 'Black oxide, zinc plated, HDG on request' }, features: ['High torque capacity in a small head', 'Grade and marking stamped', 'Hex key access in tight spaces', 'Part thread for shear joints', 'Stainless for washdown areas'], applications: ['Machine and die assembly', 'Mould and tooling', 'Automotive and trailer parts', 'Robotic and automation frames', 'Pump and gearbox mounting'], faq: ['Allen bolt or hex bolt? The socket head lets you tighten from inside the head in confined space and carries more torque per unit size, but it needs a hex key rather than a spanner.', 'Which grade should I buy? 8.8 is standard for machinery, 10.9 and 12.9 for higher preload; never mix grades in one joint without checking the design.', 'Do stainless Allen bolts gall? Yes - stainless-on-stainless threads can seize; use anti-seize or a different grade pair, and keep the tightening speed low.'] },
  { slug: 'hanger-bolts', image: '/images/products/hanger-bolts.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'hangerbolts', minOrder: '1 ton', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: 'M6-M12, 40-200 mm', standard: 'DIN 7500 style, customer drawing', material: 'C1022 carbon steel; SS304', finish: 'Zinc, HDG, plain stainless' }, features: ['Machine thread and wood thread in one bolt', 'Lag-style coarse wood end', 'Half-thread lengths to suit beams', 'Hex or round machine end', 'Used with a nut and washer'], applications: ['Joist and beam hanging', 'Pergola and carport frames', 'Solar and antenna mounting', 'Furniture and shelving', 'Sign and lighting brackets'], faq: ['How is a hanger bolt installed? Screw the wood end into the timber with a locking pair of nuts on the machine end, then remove the nuts and fix the bracket with a nut and washer.', 'Which way round? Wood thread into timber, machine thread out for the fixture; check the thread split before ordering because the two halves are not interchangeable.', 'Stainless or zinc? Stainless for exposed outdoor work and treated timber, HDG where the fixing is structural and the site is humid.'] },
  { slug: 'hex-nuts', image: '/images/products/hex-nuts.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'hexnuts', minOrder: '1 ton', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: 'M6-M24', standard: 'DIN 934 / GB/T 6170', material: 'Carbon steel grade 8/10; SS304/316', finish: 'Electro-galvanized, HDG, plain' }, features: ['Matched to 8.8 and 10.9 bolts', 'Right-hand metric thread', 'Consistent across-flats for impact tools', 'Weight-counted cartons', 'HDG to ISO 1461'], applications: ['Structural bolting', 'Machine assembly', 'Pipe supports and frames', 'Vehicle repair', 'General fabrication'], faq: ['What grade of nut goes with an 8.8 bolt? A grade 8 nut is the normal match; a lower grade nut will strip before the bolt yields and spoils the joint.', 'How are nuts counted for export? Usually by weight with a stated pieces-per-kilo figure, or boxed in 100s; ask for the count method in the quotation so site issue matches the invoice.', 'Do HDG nuts need retapping? Hot-dip galvanized nuts are often supplied overtapped so the coating does not bind on the thread; check that the nut spins freely on a coated bolt.'] },
  { slug: 'nylon-lock-nuts', image: '/images/products/nylon-lock-nuts.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'nylonlocknuts', minOrder: '1 ton', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: 'M6-M24', standard: 'DIN 985 / ISO 7040', material: 'Carbon steel grade 8; SS304/316', finish: 'Zinc, HDG, plain stainless' }, features: ['Nylon insert resists vibration', 'Reusable a limited number of times', 'No second nut or thread locker', 'Works on standard metric bolts', 'Stainless for wet areas'], applications: ['Machinery and pumps', 'Trailers and vehicle bodies', 'Scaffold and formwork', 'Solar and mounting frames', 'Fencing and gate hardware'], faq: ['How many times can a nyloc be reused? The nylon insert loses grip after a few cycles; treat it as a one-shot fastener on safety-critical joints.', 'Is a nyloc as strong as a plain nut? The proof load is similar but the nylon adds friction; check the preload requirement rather than assuming a higher grade.', 'Can it be used at high temperature? Standard nylon inserts are for roughly -30 to +80 C; above that use an all-metal lock nut.'] },
  { slug: 'spring-washers', image: '/images/products/spring-washers.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'springwashers', minOrder: '1 ton', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: 'M6-M24', standard: 'DIN 127 / GB/T 93', material: '65Mn spring steel; SS304', finish: 'Zinc, HDG, plain' }, features: ['Helical split ring', 'Consistent spring rate', 'Matched to metric bolt sizes', 'Bulk cartons by weight', 'Stainless option for wet sites'], applications: ['Machine assembly', 'Vehicle and trailer parts', 'Pumps and compressors', 'Electrical enclosures', 'General fabrication'], faq: ['Do spring washers actually stop loosening? They help on joints with vibration and thermal cycling, but they are not a substitute for correct preload; on critical joints use a lock nut or thread locker.', 'Spring washer with a flat washer? Common practice is bolt, flat washer, then spring washer under the nut to protect the surface and keep tension.', 'Which direction? The split should face the nut, and the washer should be fully compressed at final torque.'] },
  { slug: 'solar-brackets', image: '/images/products/solar-brackets.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'solarbrackets', minOrder: '1 ton', leadTime: '20-25 days', specs: { size: 'Rail 1.5-3 m, hook 200-400 mm', standard: 'Project design, 6005-T5 extrusion', material: 'Q235B HDG, aluminium 6005-T5', finish: 'HDG, mill finish aluminium' }, features: ['Roof hooks for tile and IBR sheet', 'Mid and end clamps in aluminium', 'Pre-cut rails with drilled holes', 'Wind-load design on request', 'Packed as a kit per roof'], applications: ['Rooftop solar arrays', 'Ground-mount frames', 'Carport and shade structures', 'Off-grid installations', 'Battery and inverter mounts'], faq: ['What is in a solar bracket kit? Typically rails, roof hooks or base plates, mid and end clamps, and the bolts and nuts to fix the modules - quoted per kW or per roof layout.', 'Which roof type needs which hook? Tile roofs use a curved tile hook, IBR and corrugated sheet use a straight hook fixed through the crest, and flat roofs use a base plate or ballast frame.', 'How is it shipped? Components are bundled by type and labelled per roof section, so the installer does not have to sort a mixed container on site.'] },



  { slug: 'flange-bolts', image: '/images/products/flange-bolts.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'flangebolts', minOrder: '1 ton', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: 'M8-M20, 20-150 mm', standard: 'DIN 6921 / IFI 111', material: 'Carbon steel 8.8 / 10.9; SS304', finish: 'Zinc, HDG, black oxide' }, features: ['Integrated flange replaces a washer', 'Serrated flange option for anti-loosening', 'Longer thread for thin steel', 'Common in trailer and racking builds', 'Bulk cartons by weight'], applications: ['Steel frame and racking', 'Trailer and truck body', 'Agricultural machinery', 'Conveyor and guard rails', 'Solar and mounting frames'], faq: ['Why use a flange bolt instead of a hex bolt? The flange gives the same bearing area as a washer in one part, so there is one less component to stock and lose on site, and assembly is faster.', 'Does the flange replace the washer completely? On flat steel yes. On a slotted or oversized hole the flange cannot bridge the gap, so keep a plate washer.', 'Which is normal in Africa, DIN 6921 or IFI 111? Both are common; send the drawing or state the standard, because head across-corners and thread length differ between them.'] },
  { slug: 'stud-bolts', image: '/images/products/stud-bolts.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'studbolts', minOrder: '1 ton', leadTime: '20-25 days', specs: { size: 'M12-M30, 100-1000 mm', standard: 'ASTM A193 B7 / DIN 976', material: '42CrMo alloy steel; SS304/316', finish: 'Black oxide, zinc, HDG' }, features: ['Fully threaded, cut to length', 'Two nuts supplied per stud', 'B7 for high-temperature flanges', 'Marked heat number on request', 'Bundle packed by length'], applications: ['Pipe and valve flanges', 'Steel column splices', 'Pressure vessels', 'Mining and plant maintenance', 'Structural bolting'], faq: ['Stud bolt or hex bolt? A stud is used where both ends must be tightened or where the joint is opened regularly - flanges, manways and heavy splices. A hex bolt is cheaper for one-sided assembly.', 'What does A193 B7 mean? It is a chromium-molybdenum steel stud for high-temperature and high-pressure service, normally paired with an A194 2H nut; grade 8.8 is the cheaper general structural substitute.', 'How is length measured? End to end including both chamfers, with the thread running the full length - state the assembled length and the nut count you need.'] },
  { slug: 'machine-screws', image: '/images/products/machine-screws.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'machinescrews', minOrder: '500 kg', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: 'M4-M12, 8-100 mm', standard: 'DIN 7985 / 965 / 933', material: 'Carbon steel 4.8; SS304/316', finish: 'Zinc, nickel, plain stainless' }, features: ['Pan, countersunk and hex heads', 'Slotted, Phillips and hex drive', 'Fine pitch for thin metal', 'Stainless for panels and washdown', 'Small packs or bulk cartons'], applications: ['Electrical enclosures', 'Control panels', 'Sheet metal assemblies', 'Furniture hardware', 'Instrument and pump covers'], faq: ['Machine screw or self-tapping screw? A machine screw needs a pre-formed thread - a nut, a tapped hole or a threaded insert. Self-tapping cuts its own thread in sheet metal or plastic.', 'Which head for panels? Pan head for general fixing, countersunk where the surface must stay flush, hex head where higher torque is needed.'] },
  { slug: 'rivet-nuts', image: '/images/products/rivet-nuts.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'rivetnuts', minOrder: '500 kg', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: 'M4-M10, grip 0.5-3.0 mm', standard: 'DIN 7338 style', material: 'Steel, aluminium, SS304', finish: 'Zinc, plain aluminium, plain stainless' }, features: ['Thread in thin sheet, one side access', 'Flat head, countersunk and small head', 'Set with a hand or pneumatic tool', 'Steel for structural panels', 'Stainless for outdoor cabinets'], applications: ['Sheet metal enclosures', 'Automotive and trailer panels', 'HVAC and ductwork', 'Signage and display frames', 'Appliance and cabinet assembly'], faq: ['What is a rivet nut for? It puts a reusable machine thread into sheet too thin to tap, working from one side only - common on cabinets, duct and vehicle panels.', 'Which material for outdoor use? Stainless rivet nuts in stainless or aluminium sheet for outdoor cabinets; steel rivet nuts are fine indoors and cost less.'] },
  { slug: 'flange-nuts', image: '/images/products/flange-nuts.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'flangenuts', minOrder: '1 ton', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: 'M6-M20', standard: 'DIN 6923', material: 'Carbon steel 8/10; SS304', finish: 'Zinc, HDG, plain stainless' }, features: ['Wide flange spreads clamp load', 'Serrated face resists vibration', 'One part instead of nut plus washer', 'Matched to flange and hex bolts', 'Weight-counted packing'], applications: ['Steel frames and racking', 'Trailer bodies', 'Agricultural equipment', 'Solar mounting', 'General fabrication'], faq: ['Flange nut or nut plus washer? The flange covers the washer function on flat steel, so it saves a component; on aluminium or soft surfaces keep a plain washer to protect the face.', 'Do serrated flange nuts damage the surface? Yes, the teeth bite - use smooth flange nuts where the coating must stay intact, serrated where vibration loosening is the bigger risk.'] },
  { slug: 'cap-nuts', image: '/images/products/cap-nuts.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'capnuts', minOrder: '500 kg', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: 'M6-M16', standard: 'DIN 1587', material: 'Carbon steel; SS304', finish: 'Zinc, HDG, plain stainless' }, features: ['Dome closes the exposed thread', 'No water pocket at the bolt end', 'Rounded face, no snag hazard', 'Stainless for playground and marine', 'Hex or domed top'], applications: ['Playground and furniture', 'Fencing and railing', 'Automotive trim', 'Sanitary and washdown', 'Decorative steelwork'], faq: ['When should I use a cap nut? Wherever the bolt end is exposed to people, water or dust - playgrounds, railings, furniture and outdoor steel where a plain nut would leave a wet thread tip.', 'Does the dome affect strength? The thread engagement is the same as a standard nut of that height; the dome is an extra closed head, not a weaker body.'] },
  { slug: 'wing-nuts', image: '/images/products/wing-nuts.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'wingnuts', minOrder: '500 kg', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: 'M6-M12', standard: 'DIN 315', material: 'Carbon steel; SS304', finish: 'Zinc, plain stainless' }, features: ['Hand tightening without tools', 'Two large wings for grip', 'Cast or forged options', 'Stainless for wet areas', 'Used with a plain or spring washer'], applications: ['Clamping jigs and fixtures', 'Formwork and scaffold', 'Camera and instrument mounts', 'Barbecue and outdoor gear', 'Filter and pump covers'], faq: ['How much torque can a wing nut take? Only what a hand can apply - it is for frequent manual adjustment, not for load-bearing joints. Use a hex nut where torque matters.', 'Wing nut with a washer? Yes: a plain washer protects the surface and a spring washer keeps tension when the joint is opened and closed repeatedly.'] },
  { slug: 'coupling-nuts', image: '/images/products/coupling-nuts.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'couplingnuts', minOrder: '500 kg', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: 'M8-M20, 30-100 mm', standard: 'DIN 6334 style', material: 'Carbon steel 8.8; SS304', finish: 'Zinc, HDG, plain stainless' }, features: ['Joins two studs or rods', 'Long body gives full thread engagement', 'Hex for wrench tightening', 'Used in rigging and suspension', 'Cut lengths on request'], applications: ['Threaded rod suspension', 'Rigging and tie systems', 'Scaffold and formwork ties', 'Pump and valve assembly', 'Structural connections'], faq: ['How long should a coupling nut be? At least one full nut height of thread engagement in each rod, and more where the joint takes tension - ask for the rod diameter and load.', 'Coupling nut or turnbuckle? A coupling nut joins two rods at a fixed length; a turnbuckle allows adjustment after installation.'] },
  { slug: 'ground-screws', image: '/images/products/ground-screws.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'groundscrews', minOrder: '1 ton', leadTime: '20-25 days', specs: { size: 'Dia 60-89 mm, 550-1200 mm', standard: 'Project design', material: 'Q235B / Q355B steel', finish: 'HDG to ISO 1461' }, features: ['Installed without concrete', 'Removable and reusable', 'Load tested on request', 'Helical blade matched to soil', 'Flange or threaded top options'], applications: ['Ground-mount solar', 'Fencing and barriers', 'Sign and lighting posts', 'Carports and shade', 'Temporary structures'], faq: ['When is a ground screw better than concrete? On open ground with reasonable soil, where you want to avoid curing time and excavation, or where the structure may later move - solar fields, fences and temporary sites.', 'How deep does it go? Usually 600-1000 mm depending on soil and wind load, with torque recorded during installation as a soil check.'] },
  { slug: 'lock-washers', image: '/images/products/lock-washers.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'lockwashers', minOrder: '500 kg', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: 'M6-M24', standard: 'DIN 6797 / 6798', material: 'Spring steel; SS304', finish: 'Zinc, HDG, plain' }, features: ['Teeth bite into the surface', 'External and internal tooth types', 'Thin profile, fits tight spaces', 'Stainless for wet areas', 'Bulk cartons by weight'], applications: ['Electrical panels', 'Machine guards', 'Vehicle brackets', 'Pumps and fans', 'General fabrication'], faq: ['Do toothed washers damage the coating? Yes, the teeth mark the surface - on painted or galvanized work use a plain washer under the toothed one.', 'Lock washer or nyloc nut? A toothed washer resists rotation but does not hold preload; for critical vibrating joints use a nylon lock nut or a thread-locking compound.'] },



  { slug: 'ptfe-nuts', image: '/images/products/ptfe-nuts.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'ptfenuts', minOrder: '500 kg', leadTime: '20-25 days', specs: { size: 'M6-M20, DIN934 body', standard: 'DIN 934 body + PTFE insert', material: 'Carbon steel or SS304 body; PTFE insert', finish: 'Zinc, plain stainless, green/white PTFE' }, features: ['PTFE seals as well as locks', 'Chemical and solvent resistant', 'Works on stainless and plastic pipe', 'Cleanable, no thread compound', 'Colour coded inserts available'], applications: ['Chemical and water piping', 'Food and beverage lines', 'Pump and filter housings', 'Laboratory and dosing equipment', 'Outdoor water systems'], faq: ['Why a PTFE insert instead of nylon? PTFE keeps working across a wider temperature range and resists acids, solvents and chlorine, where a nylon insert would swell or crack.', 'Does it seal like a gasket? The insert closes the thread gap and stops creep along the thread, but it is not a substitute for a proper flange gasket on pressure lines.', 'Can it be reused? Each removal degrades the seal slightly; on leak-critical lines replace the nut rather than re-torquing the same one.'] },
  { slug: 'wood-screws', image: '/images/products/wood-screws.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'woodscrews', minOrder: '1 ton', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: '3.0-6.0 mm, 12-150 mm', standard: 'DIN 7998 head, customer drawing', material: 'C1022 carbon steel; SS304', finish: 'Zinc, HDG, plain stainless' }, features: ['Countersunk head sits flush', 'Part thread pulls boards tight', 'Cross or square drive', 'Stainless for exterior timber', 'Bulk cartons by weight'], applications: ['Joinery and cabinet work', 'Decking and cladding', 'Fencing and trellis', 'Light timber framing', 'Pallets and crates'], faq: ['Wood screw or coach screw? Wood screws are for boards and light sections up to roughly 20 mm; coach screws carry structural loads and need a pilot hole and a spanner.', 'Do I need to pre-drill hardwood? Yes for dense hardwood and near the end of a board - a pilot hole slightly smaller than the core diameter prevents splitting.'] },
  { slug: 'set-screws', image: '/images/products/set-screws.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'setscrews', minOrder: '300 kg', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: 'M4-M16, 5-60 mm', standard: 'DIN 913 / 914 / 916', material: 'Carbon steel 8.8; SS304', finish: 'Black oxide, zinc, plain stainless' }, features: ['Cone, dog and flat points', 'Hex socket or slotted drive', 'No head - sits inside the part', 'Stainless for food machinery', 'Small boxes for maintenance stores'], applications: ['Shaft and collar locking', 'Pulley and sprocket fixing', 'Machine guards and covers', 'Instrument adjustment', 'Fixture and jig building'], faq: ['Which point for which job? Cone point bites into a shaft for permanent location, dog point gives a flat seat and easier removal, flat point protects a soft or finished surface.', 'Set screw or grub screw? Same part - \'grub screw\' is the common trade name in the UK and Africa, \'set screw\' in the US and in DIN catalogues.'] },
  { slug: 'eye-screws', image: '/images/products/eye-screws.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'eyescrews', minOrder: '300 kg', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: '4-12 mm, 40-200 mm', standard: 'Customer drawing', material: 'C1022 carbon steel; SS304', finish: 'Zinc, HDG, plain stainless' }, features: ['Wood thread bites into timber', 'Round eye takes rope or hook', 'Full thread to the eye', 'Stainless for outdoor posts', 'Sizes matched to rope diameter'], applications: ['Fencing and trellis ties', 'Awning and shade anchors', 'Boat and trailer lash points', 'Sign hanging', 'Garden and landscaping'], faq: ['How much load can an eye screw take? Only light, non-lifting loads - rope guides, shade anchors, ties. For overhead or safety loads use a rated eye bolt in a drilled fixing.', 'Should I pre-drill? Yes: a pilot hole about two thirds of the core diameter stops hardwood splitting and keeps the eye straight.'] },
  { slug: 'semi-tubular-rivets', image: '/images/products/semi-tubular-rivets.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'semitubularrivets', minOrder: '300 kg', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: '2.4-6.4 mm, 4-25 mm long', standard: 'DIN 7340 style', material: 'Steel, aluminium, copper, SS304', finish: 'Zinc, plain' }, features: ['Low force to set', 'No hollow head to fill', 'Consistent clinch with a press or arbor', 'Cheap per thousand', 'Colour matching in aluminium'], applications: ['Luggage and cases', 'Hand tools and hardware', 'Electrical contacts', 'Toys and small appliances', 'Sheet metal trim'], faq: ['Semi-tubular or blind rivet? Blind rivets set from one side with a hand tool and suit site work; semi-tubular rivets are cheaper per piece and set with a press in a workshop.', 'What rivet length do I need? Length should exceed the combined thickness by roughly 1 to 1.5 times the diameter so the tubular end has enough material to roll.'] },
  { slug: 'metal-brackets', image: '/images/products/metal-brackets.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'metalbrackets', minOrder: '500 kg', leadTime: '25-30 days', specs: { size: 'Thickness 1.5-6 mm, to drawing', standard: 'Customer drawing / sample', material: 'Q235, SS304, galvanized sheet', finish: 'HDG, powder coat, plain' }, features: ['Made from drawing or sample', 'Holes, slots and folds in one part', 'Powder coating to colour', 'Tolerance checked on first article', 'Packed by project or by set'], applications: ['Solar and mounting frames', 'HVAC and duct supports', 'Furniture and shelving', 'Machine guards', 'Signage and display'], faq: ['What do you need to quote a bracket? A drawing or a sample with thickness, material, hole positions and finish; a photo plus dimensions is enough for a first price.', 'How is quality controlled? First article inspection against the drawing, then a sampling check on hole position and coating thickness before packing.'] },
  { slug: 'solar-hooks', image: '/images/products/solar-hooks.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'solarhooks', minOrder: '500 kg', leadTime: '20-25 days', specs: { size: 'Hook 200-400 mm, plate 40-60 mm', standard: 'Project design', material: 'Q235B HDG; SS304', finish: 'HDG to ISO 1461' }, features: ['Curved hook for tile roofs', 'Straight hook through sheet crest', 'Adjustable height versions', 'Matched bolts and washers supplied', 'Bundled per roof section'], applications: ['Tile roof solar arrays', 'IBR and corrugated roofs', 'Carport and canopy frames', 'Solar water heating', 'Small ground frames'], faq: ['Which hook for which roof? Curved tile hooks sit under the tile on the purlin; straight hooks fix through the crest of IBR or corrugated sheet with a sealing washer.', 'Why HDG rather than painted? A roof hook is wet for years; hot-dip galvanizing gives a zinc layer that survives scrapes during installation far better than paint.'] },
  { slug: 'aluminum-profiles', image: '/images/products/aluminum-profiles.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'aluminumprofiles', minOrder: '500 kg', leadTime: '20-25 days', specs: { size: 'Rail 30-60 mm section, 1.5-3 m', standard: '6005-T5 extrusion', material: 'Aluminium 6005-T5 / 6063', finish: 'Mill, anodized, powder coated' }, features: ['Light and corrosion free', 'Slotted rail takes clamps anywhere', 'Cut and drilled to layout', 'Bundled and labelled per roof', 'Matches our clamps and hooks'], applications: ['Solar module rails', 'Framing and display systems', 'Guard and barrier supports', 'Machine frames', 'Sign structures'], faq: ['Why 6005-T5 rather than 6063? 6005-T5 is the common solar rail alloy with higher strength after tempering; 6063 is fine for light framing and costs less.', 'Anodized or mill finish? Mill finish is acceptable inland; anodizing or powder coating is worth it on coastal sites where salt spray dulls the surface.'] },
  { slug: 'solar-clamps', image: '/images/products/solar-clamps.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'solarclamps', minOrder: '500 kg', leadTime: '20-25 days', specs: { size: 'For 30-40 mm frame, M8 bolt', standard: 'Project design', material: 'Aluminium 6005-T5; SS304 bolts', finish: 'Mill, anodized' }, features: ['Mid clamp joins two modules', 'End clamp closes the array edge', 'Anodized against salt spray', 'Set packing speeds installation', 'Matches our rails and hooks'], applications: ['Rooftop solar arrays', 'Ground-mount frames', 'Carports', 'Solar water heating', 'Small off-grid kits'], faq: ['Mid clamp or end clamp? Mid clamps hold two adjacent modules on one rail; end clamps hold the outer edge of the last module and are sized to the frame thickness.', 'How many sets per kW? Roughly 10 to 12 clamp sets per kW on a standard portrait layout, but count by rail length and module width rather than by rule of thumb.'] },
  { slug: 'steel-channels', image: '/images/products/steel-channels.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'steelchannels', minOrder: '1 ton', leadTime: '20-25 days', specs: { size: 'C 80-200 mm, thickness 1.5-3 mm', standard: 'EN 10346 / project design', material: 'Galvanized steel S250GD-S350GD', finish: 'Zinc coated, pre-galvanized' }, features: ['Cold-formed, light and stiff', 'Cut and punched to layout', 'Galvanized inside and out', 'Stacks flat for container loading', 'Used as purlin or frame'], applications: ['Roof purlins', 'Light steel frames', 'Solar ballast frames', 'Partition studs', 'Racking and shelving'], faq: ['C channel or welded frame? Cold-formed C sections are lighter and cheaper for purlins and light frames; welded sections are used where loads and spans are larger.', 'How is coating specified? State the zinc mass (for example Z275) or the exposure class; coastal sites need a heavier coating or a painted system on top.'] },

  { slug: 'plastic-anchors', image: '/images/products/plastic-anchors.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'plasticanchors', minOrder: '300 kg', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: '5-14 mm × 25-75 mm', standard: 'Factory spec (PA6)', material: 'Nylon PA6 / PP', finish: 'White, blue, grey' }, features: ['Four-lip expansion', 'Matches standard self-tapping screws', 'Colour-coded by size', 'Boxed 100-1,000 pcs', 'Works in concrete, block and tile'], applications: ['Concrete and block walls', 'Tile and drywall fixing', 'Skirting and trunking', 'Bathroom fittings', 'General building work'], faq: ['Which plug size for which screw? Match the plug to the screw: a 5 mm plug takes a 3-3.5 mm screw, 8 mm takes 4-5 mm, 10 mm takes 6 mm, 14 mm takes 8 mm. The plug must be slightly larger than the drill hole so it grips.', 'Concrete, block or hollow brick? The same plug works in all three, but holding power falls sharply in hollow block and aerated block. In hollow block use a longer plug that bridges the cavity, or a chemical anchor for anything load-bearing.', 'How deep should I drill? Drill about 5-10 mm deeper than the plug length so dust does not stop the plug short, then blow the hole clean. A plug sitting proud of the surface will not hold the fixture tight.', 'Can I use plastic anchors outdoors? Yes for light loads, but use the grey or UV-stabilised grades. In coastal or exposed sites, plastic ages faster than steel - use a mechanical or chemical anchor for anything structural.', 'Do you supply wall plugs to Africa? Yes - colour-coded boxes of 100-1,000 pcs, mixed sizes per carton, 15-25 days by sea to Beira or Durban.'] },
  { slug: 'drywall-anchors', image: '/images/products/drywall-anchors.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'drywallanchors', minOrder: '300 kg', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: '3.5-4.8 mm × 25-40 mm', standard: 'Factory spec / EN 14566 accessories', material: 'Nylon PA6 body, zinc-plated screw', finish: 'White, blue' }, features: ['Self-drilling into plasterboard', 'No stud needed', 'Screw re-usable in the same anchor', 'Zinc-plated screw included', 'Boxed 100-500 pcs'], applications: ['Plasterboard walls', 'Hollow and cavity walls', 'Shelving and mirrors', 'Picture and TV brackets', 'Trunking and cable trays'], faq: ['How much can a drywall anchor hold? A 4 mm self-drilling anchor in 12.5 mm plasterboard typically holds 10-20 kg in shear per anchor. That is shelf, mirror and bracket territory - not overhead lifting or safety-critical loads.', 'Will it work in 9.5 mm board? Yes, but drive it slowly and do not over-tighten; thin board tears if the anchor is forced. For heavy items, use two anchors rather than one larger one.', 'Can I remove and refit the screw? Yes - unlike a plug that drops into the cavity, the self-drilling anchor stays in the board, so the screw can be taken out and refitted several times.', 'What if I hit a stud? Stop and use a normal wood or metal screw into the stud - a stud fixing is always stronger than an anchor in board.', 'Do you supply drywall anchors to Africa? Yes - boxed 100-500 pcs with screws, mixed sizes per carton, 15-25 days by sea.'] },
  { slug: 'j-bolts', image: '/images/products/j-bolts.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'jbolts', minOrder: '200 pcs', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: 'M8-M24 × 100-600 mm', standard: 'DIN 529 / ASTM F1554 on request', material: 'Q235 / Q345 carbon steel', finish: 'Hot-dip galvanized, zinc plated' }, features: ['Hooked end anchors into concrete', 'Nut and washer supplied', 'Custom hook radius and length', 'HDG for outdoor use', 'Bundled by size'], applications: ['Fence posts and poles', 'Precast and foundation fixing', 'Roof and canopy anchors', 'Transmission pole bases', 'Temporary works'], faq: ['What is a J bolt used for? The hooked end is cast into concrete or set in a foundation, and the threaded leg takes a nut to hold a post, pole or frame. It is the standard fixing for fence posts, light poles and precast panels.', 'J bolt or U bolt? A J bolt anchors one leg into a base; a U bolt wraps around a pipe or pole and fixes it to a support. If the item is set into concrete, use a J bolt; if it is clamped to something, use a U bolt.', 'How long should the bolt be? Length = embedment in concrete plus the thickness of the part being fixed plus room for the nut and washer. Typical embedment is 150-300 mm for posts and 300 mm and above for poles.', 'Galvanized or plain? Hot-dip galvanized for anything exposed outdoors or in the ground; plain or zinc-plated only for dry, internal or grouted conditions.', 'Do you supply J bolts to Zimbabwe and Zambia? Yes - M8 to M24, HDG, cut to length, 15-25 days by sea to Beira or Durban.'] },
  { slug: 'binding-wire', image: '/images/products/binding-wire.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'bindingwire', minOrder: '1 ton', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: '0.7-2.5 mm × 25 kg coil', standard: 'GB/T 343 / EN 10244 coating', material: 'Q195 low-carbon steel', finish: 'Electro galvanized, black annealed' }, features: ['Soft enough to tie by hand', '25 kg coils, poly-wrapped', 'Galvanized or black annealed', 'Consistent diameter', 'Loads flat in the container'], applications: ['Rebar tying', 'Blockwork and brickwork', 'Fencing and trellis', 'Bundling and packing', 'Formwork ties'], faq: ['What diameter for rebar? 0.9-1.2 mm is the usual rebar tying wire; 1.6-2.0 mm for heavier bar and precast; 0.7-0.9 mm for light bundling and packing.', 'Galvanized or black annealed? Black annealed is cheaper and softer, fine indoors or where it is covered by concrete. Galvanized holds up outdoors and in damp blockwork, at a higher price.', 'How much wire per tonne of rebar? Roughly 8-12 kg per tonne of rebar depending on bar size and spacing - order by the coil and keep a spare on site rather than calculating to the last kilo.', 'Is the coil weight exact? Coils are nominal 25 kg; accept a small tolerance and check on a scale at receipt if the order is large.', 'Do you supply binding wire to Africa? Yes - 25 kg coils, galvanized or black, 15-25 days by sea to Beira or Durban.'] },
  { slug: 'roofing-screws', image: '/images/products/roofing-screws.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'roofingscrews', minOrder: '500 kg', leadTime: '15-20 days', specs: { size: '4.2-6.3 mm × 50-150 mm', standard: 'DIN 7504K / project spec', material: 'C1022 carbon steel', finish: 'Ruspert, HDG, zinc plated' }, features: ['Hex washer head with EPDM seal', 'Self-drilling TEK point', 'Colour matched to sheet on request', 'Tested for watertight laps', 'Boxed 500-1,000 pcs'], applications: ['IBR and corrugated roofing', 'Insulated sandwich panels', 'Metal wall cladding', 'Solar mounting', 'Warehouse and factory roofs'], faq: ['Which screw for an IBR roof? A TEK 3 self-drilling screw with an EPDM washer, typically 12-14 × 65-75 mm, long enough to penetrate the purlin by at least 25 mm. Match the length to sheet plus purlin thickness.', 'Why the EPDM washer? The washer compresses under the head and seals the hole against rain and capillary action. A screw without a washer leaks at every fixing, however well it is driven.', 'Should the screw go through the crest or the pan? Through the crest for a clean fixing and less trapped water; on some profiles the pan is specified. Follow the sheet manufacturer and stay consistent across the roof.', 'Ruspert or HDG? Ruspert is an alkaline-resistant multi-layer coating used where the roof sees acid rain, coastal air and animal waste; HDG is the cheaper standard for inland roofs. Both outlast plain zinc.', 'Do you supply roofing screws to Africa? Yes - with and without washers, in sheet colours, 500-1,000 pcs per box, 15-25 days by sea.'] },
  { slug: 'chemical-anchors', image: '/images/products/chemical-anchors.jpg', pricePerPiece: 0, nameKey: 'chemicalanchors', minOrder: '300 pcs', leadTime: '20-25 days', specs: { size: 'M8-M24 × 110-300 mm', standard: 'ETA assessment on request', material: 'Zinc-plated carbon steel / SS316 rod', finish: 'Zinc plated, plain stainless' }, features: ['Glass capsule, no mixing', 'Fast cure in normal temperatures', 'Heavy loads in concrete', 'Stainless rod option for coastal', 'Supplied as a complete kit'], applications: ['Curtain wall and facade', 'Machine and equipment bases', 'Steel column fixings', 'Seismic and retrofit anchors', 'Bridge and infrastructure works'], faq: ['What is a chemical anchor? A resin capsule is spun in the drilled hole, breaking the glass and mixing the components; the rod is then pushed in and the resin cures around it, bonding to the full hole wall instead of gripping at one point.', 'When is chemical better than mechanical? In cracked concrete, close to edges, in wet or flooded holes, and for heavy vibration loads. A mechanical wedge anchor concentrates stress and can split the base in those conditions.', 'What is the cure time? Typically 20-40 minutes at 20-25 °C and longer below 10 °C; do not load the anchor until the full cure time has passed. Cold weather and damp holes extend it further.', 'Can the capsule be shipped? Yes, but glass capsules need care in packing and are normally shipped in their cartons with the rods separate. Tell us the destination and we pack accordingly.', 'Do you supply chemical anchors to Africa? Yes - capsule kits M8-M24 with rod, nut and washer, 20-25 days by sea.'] },
]

